It works a bit like control, 

- Traverses the screen list in IntuitionBase searching for a MAXS screen
  or MAXS window of the required node number.  

- Finds the IDCMP port associated with the MAXS screen/window.

- Opens up a reply message port, (for replies from the IDCMP port).

- Sends a "MENUPICK" fake IDCMP message to the MAXS IDCMP port, with the
  corresponding "MENUITEM", ie sleep, twit etc.

- If "MENUITEM" is "LOGOUTPUT" it waits a second or so, and once again
  traverses the window list, searching for a "Printer/Output" window.

- It then traverses the gadget list of the "Printer/Output" window, searching
  for a gadget with a StringInfo structure, (ie a string gadget).  

- This string gadget is then removed from the "Printer/Output" windows gadget
  list, having it's internal buffers modified to contain whatever string you
  pass in the args as the log file.

- The string gadget is then added back on to the "Printer/Output" windows'
  gadget list and the list is refreshed.  As long as the file can be opened,
  everything from then on is logged into the file!


So waddya think?  ;-)


*NOTE*

1: You must have the screen open, ie not iconified for this to work, if it
   is iconified it'll most likely crash!

2: There must be someone logged in!  If you want to run this automatically
   without having to be around to make it work, you'll have to write a 
   little door, (ADOS script/Hisoft/etc), that calls this ute with the
   correct parameters as part of "introdoor.text"/"maindoor.text"/etc.
   Then call the ute with the same parameters as part of your logoff
   sequence!

3: You must rename "libs:reqtools.library" to a different name and then
   reboot to have any hope whatsoever in having this work!  (This means
   that while you have "reqtools.library" renamed that any program that uses
   "reqtools.library" will cease to work in the same way that it did!

4: To stop the logging, either just manually select the "Printer/Output"
   "MENUITEM" or run the ute with the same parameters.

5: Please do NOT give this to anyone else, as it is a hack of the highest
   order and I do not want something this dangerous spread around!

6: To run it, it's the same as control apart from having one extra option,
   "LOGOUTPUT", when using this option you also need to specify an extra
   parameter. "FILE", which is the path/name of the log file.

eg: Control 1 LOGOUTPUT ram:user.log


